# E10. walker simulate --arms --lift --script test/sim/lift/02-hold-release-stop.walk
# SIMULATED lift board (src/sim/fakeLift.ts) and SIMULATED arms, the real lift client under the real motion
# coordinator. `lift-hold-on` / `lift-hold-off` play the screen's hold control (a "still held" every 50 ms, as the
# page sends it); every lift motion is prepared (as the terminal does) and started by the Confirm press `c`.
# Real time: about 45 s.

expect lift state unhomed
expect motion mode ready
# The SIMULATED arms start folded at "stowed": their motors go on, so they count as stowed.
key torque-on-left
wait 2100
key c
expect motion torque left on
key torque-on-right
wait 2100
key c
expect motion torque right on

# Confirm with nothing held: refused, nothing moves.
key lift-home
wait 2100
key c
expect motion command lift.home refused:not_held operator_cli

# Home while holding the screen's lift control.
key lift-hold-on
expect lift hold on
key lift-home
expect motion target lift.home operator_cli: Home the lift
wait 2100
key c
expect motion command lift.home started operator_cli
expect motion lift accepted lift.home
expect 40000 motion lift ended lift.home completed

# Raise, and let go partway: it ramps down and stops, still homed, and never resumes.
key lift-up
expect motion target lift.move operator_cli: Raise the lift to 300 mm
wait 2100
key c
expect motion lift accepted lift.move
wait 3000
key lift-hold-off
expect 2000 motion lift ended lift.move stopped
expect motion command lift.move stopped operator_cli

# Raise again; a Talk press mid-move stops it.
key lift-hold-on
key lift-up
wait 2100
key c
expect motion lift accepted lift.move
wait 1000
key t
expect motion stop handle_press
expect 2000 motion lift ended lift.move stopped

# Again; the stop switch mid-move stops the arms and the lift, which both latch stop_circuit_opened.
key lift-up
wait 2100
key c
expect motion lift accepted lift.move
wait 1000
key lift-stop-switch
expect motion fault stop_circuit_opened system
expect 2000 motion lift ended lift.move failed stop_circuit_opened
expect motion fault stop_circuit_opened lift
key lift-clear
expect motion command fault.clear refused:cause_present operator_cli
key lift-stop-switch
wait 500
key lift-clear
wait 2100
key c
expect 2000 motion lift clear cleared
expect motion mode ready

# The stop cut the arms' power (they are limp) and unhomed the lift: the motors go on again, and a move is then
# refused until it homes again.
key torque-on-left
wait 2100
key c
expect motion torque left on
key torque-on-right
wait 2100
key c
expect motion torque right on
key lift-up
expect motion command lift.move refused:lift_not_homed operator_cli
key q
